      "notes": "<h2>Chemical Bonding</h2>\n<h3> WELL EXPLAINED NOTES</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Chemical bonding is the force of attraction that holds atoms together in a molecule or compound.</li>\n<li>Atoms bond to achieve a stable electronic configuration (usually a full outer shell).</li>\n<li>Stability is achieved by gaining, losing, or sharing electrons.</li>\n<li>Main types of bonding: Ionic bonding, Covalent bonding, Metallic bonding.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3> TYPES OF BONDING (SIMPLIFIED)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Ionic bonding:</b> Transfer of electrons (metal + non-metal)</li>\n<li><b>Covalent bonding:</b> Sharing of electrons (non-metal + non-metal)</li>\n<li><b>Metallic bonding:</b> Sea of free electrons in metals</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3> SIMPLE MODEL</h3>\n<pre>\nAtoms → Electron change → Stable compound\n</pre>\n",
