      "notes": "<h2>Chemical Equations</h2>\n<h3> WELL EXPLAINED NOTES</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>A chemical equation is a symbolic representation of a chemical reaction.</li>\n<li>It shows reactants on the left and products on the right.</li>\n<li>Arrows indicate the direction of the reaction.</li>\n<li>Coefficients are used to balance equations.</li>\n<li>Chemical equations must obey the Law of Conservation of Mass.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3> KEY TERMS</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><b>Reactants:</b> Starting substances in a reaction</li>\n<li><b>Products:</b> New substances formed after reaction</li>\n<li><b>Arrow (→):</b> Means “yields” or “produces”</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3> SIMPLE MODEL</h3>\n<pre>\nReactants  →  Products\nMg + O₂     →  MgO\n</pre>\n\n<h3> EXAMPLE WITH BALANCING</h3>\n<pre>\nUnbalanced: Mg + O₂ → MgO\nBalanced:   2Mg + O₂ → 2MgO\n</pre>\n",
